00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:50.290
So I think that those are those are things
that we as a society and as a nation need

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:56.500
to consciously combat and pay attention to,
because I know someone that we're covered

00:11:56.500 --> 00:12:02.810
from Kofod four months ago is not going to
give you the virus, but people are still afraid.

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:07.990
It seems I'm one of the ways where the stigma
is is entering a little more is with some

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:13.930
of the reports that, for example, of the younger
people that are dying overwhelmingly, they

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:21.720
are obese and obesity is often associated
with, you know, moral failings rather than

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:22.720
medical conditions.

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:26.070
So it seems maybe that's one way in which
it's creeping in lately.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:27.970
Oh, yeah.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:30.860
I actually started my first year and a half.

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:31.860
I was in public health.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:38.360
I was doing research on obesity stigma, and
I found infectious disease to be a less depressing

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:39.360
topic.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.710
And it tells you something about how bad it
is.

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:42.710
Yeah.

00:12:42.710 --> 00:12:44.050
I think that absolutely.

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:51.260
A lot of the things about preexisting conditions
are allowing people to blame those who've

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:57.320
died of covered for their own deaths, which
is deeply frustrating.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:13:02.980
You know, most of the most of the preexisting
conditions that really predispose people to

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:10.730
dying from Koven are those that are really
frequently linked to structural factors in

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:17.769
economics, in race and access to medical care
